onomer. Homodimer after ligand binding. Interacts predominantly with FGF1 and FGF2, but can also interact with FGF3, FGF4, FGF6, FGF7, FGF8, FGF9, FGF10, FGF17, FGF18 and FGF22 (in vitro). Ligand specificity is determined by tissue-specific expression of isoforms, and differences in the third Ig-like domain are crucial for ligand specificity. Isoform 1 has high affinity for FGF1 and FGF2, but low affinity for FGF7. Isoform 3 has high affinity for FGF1 and FGF7, and has much higher affinity for FGF7 than isoform 1 (in vitro). Affinity for fibroblast growth factors (FGFs) is increased by heparan sulfate glycosaminoglycans that function as coreceptors. Likewise, KLB increases the affinity for FGF19 and FGF21. Interacts with PLCG1, GRB2 and PAK4. Interacts with FLRT2 (By similarity)"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"P21802-2","name":"2","synonyms":["Short"],"notes":[],"length":768,"transcripts":{"ensembl":[],"refseq":[],"refseqProteins":[],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,767]],"edits":[{"start":768,"end":821,"original":"EYLDLSQPLEQYSPSYPDTRSSCSSGDDSVFSPDPMPYEP","replacement":"I","added":1}],"missing":54,"replaced":0,"novel":1,"foldedAbsent":0,"foldedMissing":0,"features":[[18,54,0],[20,3,0],[30,1,0],[31,1,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-P21802-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-P21802-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":76.4,"plddt":[[0,45],[50,1],[70,18],[50,4],[70,3],[90,3],[70,9],[90,1],[70,7],[90,3],[70,6],[90,7],[70,4],[50,3],[70,5],[90,2],[70,4],[50,1],[0,22],[50,1],[70,3],[90,5],[70,14],[50,1],[70,2],[90,24],[70,5],[50,2],[70,1],[90,4],[70,3],[90,5],[70,8],[90,20],[70,3],[50,5],[70,3],[90,2],[70,2],[90,18],[70,3],[50,3],[70,3],[90,6],[70,15],[90,1],[70,4],[50,2],[0,2],[50,3],[70,4],[90,19],[70,6],[90,10],[70,3],[50,1],[0,7],[50,3],[70,10],[90,2],[70,10],[50,4],[0,6],[50,1],[0,58],[50,2],[70,3],[90,15],[70,3],[50,4],[70,2],[90,25],[70,12],[90,1],[70,2],[90,2],[70,1],[90,39],[70,2],[90,1],[70,2],[50,5],[0,5],[50,4],[7